# expect: ok
# stdout:
#   true
# __release at rc=0 frees the block — including its 8-byte refcount prefix — back
# to the allocator's free list, so the next same-size allocation reuses it
# instead of bumping the heap. __heapPtr (the bump high-water) is therefore
# unchanged across the release + re-alloc. Validates free-at-zero end to end.
# 
# The released value is an UNBOUND temporary, not a `var`: a tracked binding is
# also auto-released at scope exit (RC, plan 113), so manually `__release`-ing it
# would double-free. Releasing a fresh temp frees it exactly once, keeping this
# fixture clean under the `FAI_RC_CHECK` checked-mode.
def main
    @return Void
do
    __release([9 8 7])
    let h1 = __heapPtr()
    let c = [6 5 4]
    let h2 = __heapPtr()
    print(h1 == h2)
end
